WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.508 --> 00:00:16.858
"The Beast of the Zann echoed.

2
00:00:16.878 --> 00:00:17.959
"What's that?"

3
00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:21.141
He didn't recognize the creature from his parents' books.

4
00:00:21.462 --> 00:00:24.524
And he was sure he'd remember something that looked like that!

5
00:00:24.544 --> 00:00:28.687
"It's the most horrible beast in all the worlds."

6
00:00:29.047 --> 00:00:29.768
Wyssa shuddered.

7
00:00:30.536 --> 00:00:35.599
"How was Morb able to transport it from its home on Narakan?"

8
00:00:35.619 --> 00:00:38.761
"Narakan?" Venna sounded startled.

9
00:00:38.781 --> 00:00:40.882
"I thought that world was only a myth."

10
00:00:40.902 --> 00:00:44.283
"Apparently not," Wyssa said.

11
00:00:44.984 --> 00:00:51.247
The creature hissed, and a dark, viscous substance dripped from its jaws and sizzled on the stone bridge.

12
00:00:51.267 --> 00:00:54.229
"How big is that thing, anyway?"

13
00:00:54.389 --> 00:00:57.611
Perda cried as the enormous head rose even higher.

14
00:00:57.631 --> 00:00:59.892
"Big!" Zann answered.

15
00:01:00.308 --> 00:01:03.009
"And it doesn't seem to be in a good mood either!"

16
00:01:04.029 --> 00:01:06.550
The Beast let out a hoarse, echoing cry.

17
00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:10.831
Then its head snaked toward Zann and the others.

18
00:01:10.851 --> 00:01:13.412
"Run!" Venna shouted.

19
00:01:14.232 --> 00:01:15.152
The humans scattered.

20
00:01:15.753 --> 00:01:20.374
Zann lunged toward the gate and skidded across the rough stone on his hands and knees.

21
00:01:23.955 --> 00:01:26.936
When he glanced back, the Beast was raising its head again.

22
00:01:32.256 --> 00:01:35.958
Zann noticed that the dark goo wasn't coming from its mouth after all.

23
00:01:36.659 --> 00:01:38.160
It was oozing out of its head.

24
00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:39.760
"Look out!"

25
00:01:39.921 --> 00:01:40.621
Gliss screamed.

26
00:01:40.641 --> 00:01:42.682
"It's going to strike again!"

27
00:01:43.483 --> 00:01:46.624
Spurting angry flames, Zing flew toward the Beast.

28
00:01:46.644 --> 00:01:48.185
"Zing, no!"

29
00:01:48.405 --> 00:01:49.026
Zann shouted.

30
00:01:49.046 --> 00:01:50.627
"It's going to eat you!"

31
00:01:51.227 --> 00:01:53.048
The Beast snapped at the small dragon.

32
00:01:53.408 --> 00:01:54.729
Zing barely escaped.

33
00:01:54.749 --> 00:01:57.271
"We have to zap away!"

34
00:01:57.491 --> 00:01:59.432
Gliss cried, grabbing Darb's hand.

35
00:02:01.333 --> 00:02:02.313
"No!" Wyssa said.

36
00:02:02.333 --> 00:02:04.915
"That's the worst thing we can do.

37
00:02:05.736 --> 00:02:13.061
If the legends are true, the Beast can catch hold of Transport spells and pull its victims back—straight

38
00:02:13.281 --> 00:02:14.642
into its jaws."

39
00:02:14.662 --> 00:02:16.824
"So we're trapped?"

40
00:02:17.584 --> 00:02:20.987
Perda snapped her fingers, and a sword appeared in her hand.

41
00:02:21.007 --> 00:02:23.228
"Then we'll have to fight."

42
00:02:24.129 --> 00:02:25.710
Zann stared at her for a second.

43
00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:28.032
When had Perda become so brave?

44
00:02:29.068 --> 00:02:33.309
He couldn't imagine any other kid his age facing down a monster so calmly.

45
00:02:33.949 --> 00:02:35.870
But this was no time to think about such things.

46
00:02:36.470 --> 00:02:39.231
Rubbing his hands together, Zann conjured his own sword.

47
00:02:39.251 --> 00:02:42.051
"Stand back, kids," Venna called.

48
00:02:42.071 --> 00:02:43.832
"I'm going to blast it."

49
00:02:44.652 --> 00:02:45.892
"Wait," Wyssa said.

50
00:02:45.912 --> 00:02:49.653
"I don't think that will—" Blast!

51
00:02:50.634 --> 00:02:53.174
A bolt of energy shot out of Venna's hands.

52
00:02:53.615 --> 00:02:55.195
It flew straight at the Beast.

53
00:02:55.915 --> 00:02:58.836
The Beast opened its giant mouth Gulp!

54
00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:04.682
"Did the Beast just eat the Blast spell?"

55
00:03:04.902 --> 00:03:05.482
Gliss cried.

56
00:03:06.262 --> 00:03:10.604
Zann didn't have time to answer as he dodged another sizzling drop of slime.

57
00:03:11.304 --> 00:03:14.606
He found himself beside Darb, who was still cradling the mibbit.

58
00:03:14.626 --> 00:03:18.567
"The mibbit doesn't seem too worried," Zann commented.

59
00:03:19.328 --> 00:03:20.048
Darb nodded.

60
00:03:20.068 --> 00:03:24.230
"Vee told us the effects of the ear-rubbing would last a few hours, remember?"

61
00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:24.750
he said.

62
00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:25.950
"Too bad.

63
00:03:26.291 --> 00:03:29.252
I bet the mibbit was the only thing holding the Beast back before."

64
00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:31.161
"You're probably right.

65
00:03:31.581 --> 00:03:34.382
No wonder the mibbit was tense with that thing around."

66
00:03:35.203 --> 00:03:36.123
Zann glanced up.

67
00:03:36.143 --> 00:03:36.964
"Get back!"

68
00:03:38.184 --> 00:03:40.426
He and Darb leaped away in opposite directions.

69
00:03:41.146 --> 00:03:44.628
The Beast's head slammed down, shaking the whole bridge.

70
00:03:45.388 --> 00:03:47.990
"Hurry! Run while it's stunned!"

71
00:03:48.190 --> 00:03:48.790
Perda shouted.

72
00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:52.172
"Maybe it won't be able to climb out of that pit and chase us."

73
00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:54.173
Zann sprinted for the gate.

74
00:03:54.873 --> 00:03:59.616
He was only halfway there when a shimmering wall of magic energy shot up in front of him.

75
00:04:00.524 --> 00:04:01.164
"What's that?"

76
00:04:01.404 --> 00:04:01.964
Venna cried.

77
00:04:02.585 --> 00:04:03.525
Zann didn't answer.

78
00:04:03.805 --> 00:04:07.366
He lowered his head and ran straight toward the magical wall.

79
00:04:08.046 --> 00:04:10.347
But he bounced off it and stumbled into Darb.

80
00:04:11.007 --> 00:04:12.167
"Oof," Darb grunted.

81
00:04:12.927 --> 00:04:15.848
He fell backward, almost slipping off the edge of the bridge.

82
00:04:16.488 --> 00:04:18.989
To catch himself, he had to drop the mibbit.

83
00:04:19.589 --> 00:04:24.391
The fuzzy creature landed on its feet and just stood there, flicking its ears lazily.

84
00:04:24.411 --> 00:04:26.051
"Look out!"

85
00:04:26.191 --> 00:04:26.731
Perda yelled.

86
00:04:26.751 --> 00:04:29.192
"The Beast is coming for you guys!"

87
00:04:30.376 --> 00:04:33.078
Zann grabbed Darb and dragged him away from the Beast.

88
00:04:33.858 --> 00:04:40.562
The Beast's orange eyes glowed, and another wall of magic energy sprang up inside the first.

89
00:04:41.422 --> 00:04:42.983
"Why did it make another wall?

90
00:04:43.703 --> 00:04:46.024
The first one seemed to be working pretty well."

91
00:04:46.845 --> 00:04:48.706
Zann winced, touching his shoulder.

92
00:04:49.426 --> 00:04:53.288
He would definitely have a bruise to heal later—if he survived this.

93
00:04:53.308 --> 00:04:56.850
"I think it's herding us back toward itself."

94
00:04:57.731 --> 00:05:00.052
Suddenly Perda looked scared.

95
00:05:00.488 --> 00:05:02.650
"Look! It's drooling."

96
00:05:02.670 --> 00:05:05.372
"This is hopeless!"

97
00:05:05.693 --> 00:05:07.775
Gliss cried, her voice shaking.

98
00:05:07.795 --> 00:05:12.999
"The Beast is going to eat us, and there's nothing we can do about it!"

99
00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:15.061
Darb grabbed the mibbit.

100
00:05:15.081 --> 00:05:16.983
"Isn't there anything you can do?"

101
00:05:17.223 --> 00:05:18.464
he asked Wyssa and Venna.

102
00:05:19.445 --> 00:05:21.286
Wyssa was peering at the magic walls.

103
00:05:21.306 --> 00:05:25.230
"Let me think, let me think," she muttered.

104
00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:30.309
"There must be a way Zann glanced from Wyssa to his friends.

105
00:05:31.009 --> 00:05:33.930
Perda and Gliss were clinging to each other, looking terrified.

106
00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:36.270
Zing was hiding behind Venna.

107
00:05:36.911 --> 00:05:40.212
Darb, cradling the mibbit, was looking nervously at the Beast.

108
00:05:41.012 --> 00:05:45.253
The hideous creature was sizing them up, as if deciding whom to eat first.

109
00:05:46.273 --> 00:05:48.054
Suddenly Zann's eyes lit up.

110
00:05:48.734 --> 00:05:49.314
"I've got it!

111
00:05:49.674 --> 00:05:51.215
Everyone run toward the tower!"

112
00:05:51.235 --> 00:05:53.095
"What?" Venna said.

113
00:05:53.115 --> 00:05:54.456
"Are you crazy?"

114
00:05:55.272 --> 00:05:58.575
Zann didn't answer; he raced along the bridge toward the tower.

115
00:05:59.255 --> 00:06:00.216
Perda caught up to him.

116
00:06:00.236 --> 00:06:03.399
"Zann, the door is bolted shut!

117
00:06:04.159 --> 00:06:06.922
And we won't have time to try to open it with a spell.

118
00:06:07.642 --> 00:06:09.664
The Beast will have us cornered!"

119
00:06:09.684 --> 00:06:11.485
"Just go."

120
00:06:12.366 --> 00:06:16.489
Zann shoved her forward and then turned to make sure the others were following.

121
00:06:17.390 --> 00:06:19.111
Wyssa was the last to run past.

122
00:06:19.912 --> 00:06:21.473
She gave Zann a strange look.

123
00:06:22.074 --> 00:06:24.416
"I hope you know what you're doing, boy."

124
00:06:25.380 --> 00:06:26.501
Zann hoped so too.

125
00:06:27.302 --> 00:06:31.224
He glanced at the Beast, which was already gathering itself for another attack.

126
00:06:32.185 --> 00:06:36.268
As the huge head snaked toward him, Zann sprinted after the others.

127
00:06:37.028 --> 00:06:39.950
He could feel the creature's hot breath on the back of his neck.

128
00:06:40.671 --> 00:06:45.394
A drop of viscous goo landed on his shoulder, burning right through his shirt.

129
00:06:46.735 --> 00:06:47.936
Zann yelped in pain.

130
00:06:48.576 --> 00:06:53.960
He picked up speed, trying not to imagine the Beast's sharp teeth digging into his skin.
